			<section class="sidebarSubLinks">
  <header>
  <h2>About the City Secretary</h2>
  </header>
  
  <p><img src="images/lemon-350.jpg" alt="Troy D. Lemon" width="150" height="150" align="right" class="homeimagegraytworight">
    The   City Secretary shall be the clerk or secretary of the council, whose   duty it shall be to act as reading and recording clerk to the council   and to certify the correctness of the minutes and the journals and to   perform such other duties as may be required by the city council and the   mayor ... <a href="about.html">More ...</a></p>
</section>

        <section class="sidebarSubLinks">
  <header>
  <h2>Assistive Listening Devices</h2>
  </header>
          
          <p align="center"><img src="images/assistedlisteningdevice.png" alt="Assisted Listening Device" width="256" height="100" class="homeimagegraytwo"></p>
          <p>Assistive listening devices are available to accommodate and include those with hearing loss. Assistive listening systems amplify the sound directly from the audio source without amplifying background noise for better speech intelligibility.</p>
          <p>            If you would like to utilize an assistive listening device/receiver free of charge, please notify the City Secretary’s office when you sign up to speak at Public Session or public hearings.  If you a requesting a device during Council or Committee meetings, please check in with a city representative when you arrive. <a href="https://youtu.be/vTI8F6WPDO8">View video on how to use</a></p>
          <p>            If you have any questions, you may also contact the Mayor’s Assistance Office at 832.393.0955 or by email at <a href="mailto:OurNeighborhoods@houstontx.gov">OurNeighborhoods@houstontx.gov</a></p>
        </section>


